== Q3: is trend absent the same word as a window gap? ==
crawl_runner.py lines carrying the literal 'absent': 3
   | nobody snapshotted as today='absent'), so the gap gets a name instead of a
   | today answers 'absent' rather than 0 when no row names it - and delta is
   | 'absent' if usable else 'unmeasured')
trend.today = 2 | gap face names 11-18 among []
trend today-absent means: a row for the HEAD day is missing.
window gap means: a calendar day inside [threshold..head] holds no row.
SAME predicate (no row for that literal day), DIFFERENT faces: one day versus a set. A shared invariant is therefore expressible.

